  "step1_summary": "- Chief complaint: Acute shortness of breath and pleuritic right-sided back pain with hemoptysis.\n- Symptoms (onset, duration, severity, aggravating/alleviating factors): Acute onset today of breathlessness and right-sided pleuritic pain on deep inspiration; coughed up a small amount of blood on two occasions today; felt slightly feverish (patient felt warm by hand) and palpitations/awareness of heartbeat; 2 weeks of increased tiredness and reduced exercise tolerance prior to acute episode. Pain worse with deep inspiration and coughing. No clear alleviating factors mentioned.\n- Past medical history: Systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE).\n- Medications/allergies: Methotrexate (took this morning). No drug allergies reported.\n- Family/social history: Non-smoker; office-based work; lives alone in flat; has a cat. No family history of venous thromboembolism reported.\n- Vital signs/exam findings: Patient self-counted radial pulse ≈66–74 bpm; peripheral capillary refill appeared normal on video; throat exam visually unremarkable; patient felt warm but no measured temperature recorded; no palpable cervical lymphadenopathy by patient. No formal BP/SpO2/respiratory rate/temperature measured in the transcript.\n- Labs/imaging: None performed or reported in the transcript.",
